11. Fact Table Grain
FACT_SALES

The grain is one sales-order item.

Example:

Sales Order = 100001
Item = 10
Product = P100
Quantity = 5


represents one fact row.

FACT_INVENTORY

The grain is:

Product + Plant + Storage Location + Snapshot Date


This grain must be maintained consistently to avoid incorrect inventory aggregation.

12. Business Measures
Revenue
SUM(NET_VALUE)

Cost
SUM(COST)

Gross Profit
Revenue - Cost

Gross Margin Percentage
(Gross Profit / Revenue) × 100

Inventory Value
Stock Quantity × Unit Cost

Days of Stock
Current Stock / Average Daily Consumption

13. Analytical Design Principle

The analytical model separates:

Measures and business events into fact tables.

Descriptive business context into dimension tables.

This structure supports reusable analytical models and consistent KPI calculations.

14. Data Quality Considerations

The following conditions should be validated:

Duplicate customer identifiers

Duplicate product identifiers

Missing customer references

Missing product references

Invalid plant references

Invalid dates

Negative inventory quantities

Missing costs

Missing prices

Invalid currencies

